# 🏃 Temple Runner – Android Game

An Android endless-runner game developed through an AI-assisted development workflow, combining human creativity, AI-powered tools, and hands-on software engineering.

## 🚀 About the Project

Temple Runner is a personal game development project inspired by the endless-runner genre. The goal was to explore how modern AI development tools and agent-based workflows can help turn an idea into a working Android game.

This project represents an experiment in building software with the assistance of AI agents rather than relying entirely on traditional manual development.

## 🤖 How I Built This Project

One of the most interesting parts of this project was the development process itself.

I explored and combined several tools to make the development workflow more efficient:

- **REA (Reverse Engineering Assistant):** Used as part of my AI-assisted development and technical exploration workflow.
- **Antigravity:** Assisted with AI-powered coding, project development, and implementation.
- **Android Studio:** Used for Android development, project management, and building the application.
- **AI-assisted workflows:** Helped explore implementation approaches, solve development challenges, and iterate on the project.

Instead of treating AI as just a code generator, I explored how multiple tools could work together to support the development process.

## 🎯 Project Goals

- Explore AI-assisted game development.
- Understand how AI agents can support real software projects.
- Build an Android game from an initial concept.
- Experiment with development, debugging, and iterative improvements.
- Learn how to coordinate multiple development tools in one workflow.

## 🛠️ Development Approach

The project followed an iterative development approach:

1. Project exploration and initial setup.
2. Planning the game structure and implementation.
3. AI-assisted coding and development.
4. Testing and resolving development issues.
5. Building the Android application.
6. Preparing the project for further improvements.

## 📱 Project Status

This is an ongoing personal development project. Features, gameplay mechanics, performance, and visual improvements may continue to evolve.

## 💡 What I Learned

This project helped me explore the potential of AI-assisted engineering and how tools such as REA and Antigravity can support the process of building actual applications.

It also reinforced an important idea:

**AI is not just about generating code. It's about using the right tools, workflows, and human decisions to turn ideas into working products.**

